Gabe was terrified.
盖博当时吓坏了。

1095
00:48:50.620 --> 00:48:51.460
He had to run inside.
他不得不跑进屋里。

1096
00:48:51.940 --> 00:48:52.160
Yes.
没错。

1097
00:48:52.680 --> 00:48:58.780
And so he thought it was very interesting that Gabe still included the cockroach in his film.
所以他觉得盖博竟然还在电影里加入了蟑螂，这很有意思。

1098
00:48:59.320 --> 00:49:03.980
I'm thinking maybe the writers forgot about that scene in China.
我在想，也许编剧们忘了《中国》里的那一幕了。

1099
00:49:04.720 --> 00:49:07.240
Anthony also wondered if the writers forgot about the scene.
安东尼也想知道编剧们是不是忘了那一幕。

1100
00:49:07.560 --> 00:49:08.680
Anthony, I'm with you.
安东尼，我支持你。

1101
00:49:10.980 --> 00:49:13.020
No one is liking this movie.
没人喜欢这部电影。

1102
00:49:13.380 --> 00:49:15.080
Andy's like, turn it off.
安迪说，把它关掉。

1103
00:49:15.080 --> 00:49:17.380
Aaron is so embarrassed.
艾琳尴尬极了。

1104
00:49:17.380 --> 00:49:18.620
And she's like, I'm sorry.
她说，我很抱歉。

1105
00:49:18.820 --> 00:49:21.600
I, well, I was trying to make the party more adult.
我，嗯，我只是想让派对更成熟一点。

1106
00:49:21.860 --> 00:49:24.740
I also have this pecker poker.
我还有这个“小鸡扑克”。

1107
00:49:25.340 --> 00:49:27.340
It's the card game that gets you har.
这是一款让你硬起来的纸牌游戏。

1108
00:49:27.940 --> 00:49:30.860
It's the game of cards that gets you har.
这是一款让你硬起来的纸牌游戏。

1109
00:49:31.300 --> 00:49:31.760
Har.
硬起来。

1110
00:49:32.320 --> 00:49:32.700
Yeah.
是啊。

1111
00:49:33.320 --> 00:49:36.680
I did not Google pecker poker, just so you know,
我没有去谷歌搜索“小鸡扑克”，你要知道，

1112
00:49:36.800 --> 00:49:40.220
because I didn't want to see where the internet took me on that.
因为我不想知道互联网会把我带到什么地方去。

1113
00:49:40.400 --> 00:49:42.560
I think it's good that you didn't look it up, Angela.
我觉得你没去查是对的，安吉拉。

1114
00:49:42.560 --> 00:49:46.660
I'm not really sure where that would lead you, but probably nothing you need.
我不确定那会把你带到哪儿，但肯定没什么你需要看的。

1115
00:49:47.580 --> 00:49:48.740
Nothing I need to see.
没什么我需要看的。

1116
00:49:48.880 --> 00:49:51.980
I don't need to see what's out there when you Google pecker poker.
我不需要去看谷歌搜索“小鸡扑克”后会出现什么。

1117
00:49:52.440 --> 00:49:57.060
Well, standards and practices had some things they didn't want you to see either.
好吧，审查部门也有一些不想让你看到的东西。

1118
00:49:57.380 --> 00:49:58.220
They said, quote,
他们说，引用如下：

1119
00:50:03.100 --> 00:50:07.360
Again, do you see how polite they are?
再说一次，你看到他们有多礼貌了吗？

1120
00:50:07.440 --> 00:50:09.480
There's a please and a thank you in there.
里面还有“请”和“谢谢”。

1121
00:50:09.640 --> 00:50:10.640
They like Steve.
他们喜欢史蒂夫。

1122
00:50:10.940 --> 00:50:11.780
They clearly do.
显然是的。

1123
00:50:12.120 --> 00:50:16.240
People really liked our reaction to pecker poker, Angela.
大家真的很喜欢我们对“小鸡扑克”的反应，安吉拉。

1124
00:50:16.520 --> 00:50:20.740
Steve Burgess wrote that it made him laugh out loud when he saw our reaction.
史蒂夫·伯吉斯写道，他看到我们的反应时笑出了声。

1125
00:50:20.740 --> 00:50:29.760
Many people wanted to know if we were genuinely surprised because our reaction looks so genuine.
很多人想知道我们是否真的感到惊讶，因为我们的反应看起来太真实了。

1126
00:50:30.620 --> 00:50:33.060
But no, we knew it was coming.
但并没有，我们早就知道会发生什么。

1127
00:50:33.400 --> 00:50:34.060
I don't know.
我不知道。

1128
00:50:34.160 --> 00:50:36.100
We just gave a good reaction that day.
那天我们只是表现出了很好的反应。

1129
00:50:36.180 --> 00:50:36.620
We did.
确实。

1130
00:50:36.920 --> 00:50:37.900
So guess what?
所以你猜怎么着？

1131
00:50:38.040 --> 00:50:41.660
There's no coming back once you introduce pecker poker at work.
一旦你在工作中引入了“小鸡扑克”，就再也回不去了。

1132
00:50:41.660 --> 00:50:46.680
Immediately, the next scene is Aaron in Andy's office with Robert California.
紧接着，下一场戏是艾琳在安迪的办公室里，和罗伯特·加州在一起。

1133
00:50:46.960 --> 00:50:54.160
And he's asking her, why didn't you just ask Andy for clarification about what adult Halloween party meant?
他问她，你为什么不直接问安迪，“成人万圣节派对”到底是什么意思？

1134
00:50:54.420 --> 00:50:56.700
I mean, you guys are clearly very close.
我的意思是，你们俩显然非常亲近。

1135
00:50:56.960 --> 00:50:57.140
Yeah.
是啊。

1136
00:50:57.460 --> 00:51:00.560
And then there's that awkward look between the two of them.
然后他们俩之间出现了那种尴尬的眼神交流。

1137
00:51:00.680 --> 00:51:03.380
And Robert's like, oh, I see.
罗伯特说，哦，我明白了。

1138
00:51:03.660 --> 00:51:06.380
Well, this is now none of my business.
好吧，现在这不关我的事了。

1139
00:51:06.580 --> 00:51:07.640
But I'm going to stay.
但我打算留下来。

1140
00:51:07.860 --> 00:51:11.240
So he's going to stay and watch it all play out.
所以他打算留下来，看着这一切如何收场。

1141
00:51:11.580 --> 00:51:16.440
This is when Andy tells Aaron that the thing he wanted to tell her is that he's dating someone.
就在这时，安迪告诉艾琳，他想告诉她的事是他正在和某人约会。

1142
00:51:16.660 --> 00:51:18.880
They've gone on 31 dates.
他们已经约会了31次了。

1143
00:51:19.360 --> 00:51:26.800
And it's kind of weird because he hasn't let this woman call the office or come by the office to kind of spare Aaron's feelings.
这有点奇怪，因为他一直没让这个女人给办公室打电话或来办公室，是为了照顾艾琳的感受。

1144
00:51:26.940 --> 00:51:27.980
But now it's getting weird.
但现在情况变得有些奇怪了。

1145
00:51:28.620 --> 00:51:31.080
And so he needs to tell her.
所以他必须告诉她。

1146
00:51:31.280 --> 00:51:37.160
I thought Aaron was going to like just slowly die inside.
我以为艾琳会当场心碎而死。

1147
00:51:37.160 --> 00:51:38.920
I can't believe she even made it out the door.
我真不敢相信她竟然还能走出那扇门。

1148
00:51:39.420 --> 00:51:41.220
Ellie Kemper crushed it.
艾丽·坎伯演得太棒了。

1149
00:51:41.380 --> 00:51:41.760
She did.
确实。

1150
00:51:41.780 --> 00:51:42.700
She crushed it.
她演得太棒了。

1151
00:51:42.820 --> 00:51:44.800
I felt her heartache.
我感受到了她的心碎。

1152
00:51:44.940 --> 00:51:46.400
I felt her awkwardness.
我感受到了她的局促。

1153
00:51:46.500 --> 00:51:47.680
I felt her embarrassment.
我感受到了她的尴尬。

1154
00:51:48.320 --> 00:51:50.120
I was like, oh, poor Aaron.
我当时心想，噢，可怜的亚伦。

1155
00:51:50.660 --> 00:51:55.360
The next scene, Pam is being questioned about her ghost sighting again.
下一场戏里，帕姆又被问到了关于她看到鬼魂的事。

1156
00:51:55.920 --> 00:51:56.680
I know.
我知道。

1157
00:51:56.760 --> 00:52:04.700
I love that she called Jim out and was like, hey, how is this any different from you being superstitious about your jersey, you know, and not washing it?
我很喜欢她当面质问吉姆，说嘿，这和你迷信你的球衣、不洗球衣有什么区别，对吧？

1158
00:52:04.700 --> 00:52:10.020
Well, I want you guys to know the scene was longer and a few people take Pam's side.
嗯，我想让你们知道，原本那场戏更长一些，而且有几个人是站在帕姆这边的。

1159
00:52:10.280 --> 00:52:13.180
It was cut out, but I want you to hear it, please.
虽然被剪掉了，但我还是想让你们听听，拜托了。

1160
00:52:15.240 --> 00:52:18.580
If ghosts aren't real, how come everyone knows what they look like?
如果鬼魂不是真的，那为什么每个人都知道它们长什么样？

1161
00:52:18.640 --> 00:52:21.700
It's not like a bunch of people got together and agreed on a lie.
这又不是一群人聚在一起商量好撒谎。

1162
00:52:21.860 --> 00:52:22.400
Thank you.
谢谢。

1163
00:52:22.640 --> 00:52:23.100
Interesting.
有意思。

1164
00:52:23.940 --> 00:52:25.820
Every culture has this trope.
每个文化里都有这种桥段。

1165
00:52:26.520 --> 00:52:29.720
Clearly, there's some sort of real phenomenon out there.
显然，外面确实存在某种真实的现象。

1166
00:52:29.900 --> 00:52:31.600
Oscar, how are you on that side?
奥斯卡，你怎么站到那边去了？

1167
00:52:31.800 --> 00:52:33.100
This isn't about sides.
这不是站队的问题。

1168
00:52:33.580 --> 00:52:40.180
This is about me seeing a bluish, gray, old man in the mirror, and then he vanished.
这是关于我在镜子里看到了一个蓝灰色调的老人，然后他就消失了。

1169
00:52:40.400 --> 00:52:40.740
Pam.
帕姆。

1170
00:52:41.800 --> 00:52:42.720
This is important.
这很重要。

1171
00:52:43.500 --> 00:52:44.040
Was he me?
那是我吗？

1172
00:52:44.740 --> 00:52:45.460
Am I he?
我是他吗？

1173
00:52:46.560 --> 00:52:47.320
No, Creed.
不，克里德。

1174
00:52:47.960 --> 00:52:49.200
But that would make more sense.
但那样的话反而更说得通。

1175
00:52:52.870 --> 00:52:54.570
Luish, gray, old man.
蓝灰色调的老人。

1176
00:52:55.050 --> 00:52:56.970
And then Creed is amazing.
然后克里德的表现太棒了。

1177
00:52:57.810 --> 00:52:59.210
Tell me, Pam, was that me?
告诉我，帕姆，那是我吗？

1178
00:53:00.210 --> 00:53:07.030
But we learn in this scene that Stanley and Oscar are on the same side as Pam, and we know that Meredith is.
但我们在这场戏里了解到，斯坦利和奥斯卡是站在帕姆这边的，我们也知道梅雷迪思也是。

1179
00:53:07.210 --> 00:53:09.810
So there's more people in the office that believe in ghosts.
所以办公室里还有更多人相信鬼魂。

1180
00:53:09.810 --> 00:53:18.510
During the scene at 17 minutes and four seconds, on the light fixture behind Jim, there is a fake black crow.
在17分04秒的那场戏里，吉姆身后的灯具上有一只假的黑乌鸦。

1181
00:53:18.910 --> 00:53:20.150
It is a decoration.
那是个装饰品。

1182
00:53:20.150 --> 00:53:33.410
However, I will have you know that more than once, more than twice, I don't know why I would just catch that crow in the corner of my eye and it would make me flinch.
不过我要告诉你们，不止一次，也不止两次，我不知道为什么我总会用余光瞥见那只乌鸦，然后被它吓一跳。

1183
00:53:33.410 --> 00:53:40.950
This decoration really got to be the week we were shooting this, and I was very distracted by it during the scene.
拍摄那一周，这个装饰品真的让我很困扰，我在拍戏时被它分了心。

1184
00:53:41.070 --> 00:53:44.510
And when I saw it, it was one of those things where I was like, oh, my God, it's the crow.
当我看到它时，那种感觉就像是，噢，天哪，是那只乌鸦。

1185
00:53:45.010 --> 00:53:45.610
The crow!
那只乌鸦！

1186
00:53:45.610 --> 00:53:46.870
I remember the crow!
我记得那只乌鸦！

1187
00:53:47.190 --> 00:53:50.350
It was just like the height of it, the way it was positioned.
就是它的高度，还有它摆放的位置。

1188
00:53:50.930 --> 00:53:51.750
I don't know.
我不知道。

1189
00:53:52.030 --> 00:53:55.210
That was a personal memory that I've now shared with all of you.
那是我的一段个人记忆，现在分享给你们所有人了。

1190
00:53:56.490 --> 00:53:58.570
We got a fan question from Carolyn B.
我们收到了来自费城的卡罗琳·B发来的粉丝提问，

1191
00:53:58.770 --> 00:54:00.110
in Philadelphia who said,
她说，

1192
00:54:00.250 --> 00:54:06.750
In the spirit of this episode, I have to ask, was there ever a paranormal experience on the set of The Office?
秉承本集的主题，我必须问一下，在《办公室》的片场发生过超自然事件吗？

1193
00:54:07.610 --> 00:54:10.310
Well, Carolyn, I did not remember one.
嗯，卡罗琳，我不记得有发生过。

1194
00:54:10.750 --> 00:54:12.270
Angela, I don't know about you.
安吉拉，我不知道你那边怎么样。

1195
00:54:12.270 --> 00:54:15.230
I threw it out to The Office text thread.
我把这个问题发到了《办公室》的群聊里。

1196
00:54:15.750 --> 00:54:21.370
Yes, we have a text thread with the whole cast called The Office Peeps that we are actively on.
是的，我们有一个包含所有演员的群聊，叫“办公室伙伴”，我们一直在里面活跃。

1197
00:54:21.490 --> 00:54:23.610
It is the sweetest, most wonderful thing.
这是最贴心、最美妙的事情了。

1198
00:54:23.830 --> 00:54:25.950
I love it when we all pop up on it.
我很喜欢大家在群里冒泡的时候。

1199
00:54:26.650 --> 00:54:28.490
And Jenna put it to the group.
然后珍娜把这个问题抛给了大家。

1200
00:54:28.650 --> 00:54:34.210
Do you guys remember if we ever had a ghost or paranormal event on the set and everyone has been responding?
你们还记得我们片场有没有发生过鬼魂或超自然事件吗？大家都在回复呢。

1201
00:54:34.370 --> 00:54:38.570
The whole entire time we have been recording this podcast, our phones have been buzzing
在我们录制这期播客的整个过程中，我们的手机一直在响个不停

1202
00:54:38.570 --> 00:54:43.090
because everyone is responding and it's getting really silly.
因为每个人都在回复，情况变得非常滑稽。

1203
00:54:43.650 --> 00:54:46.370
Everyone's like, no, but now people are just kind of making up things.
大家都在说，不，但现在人们开始编造一些事情了。

1204
00:54:46.510 --> 00:54:50.450
Like Rain said, no, but it's currently haunted by the ghosts of our show.
就像雷恩说的，不，但它目前被我们节目的鬼魂缠住了。

1205
00:54:51.090 --> 00:54:53.030
And Kate Flannery said, Rain's right.
凯特·弗兰纳里说，雷恩是对的。

1206
00:54:53.130 --> 00:54:54.270
The office will never die.
《办公室》永远不会消亡。

1207
00:54:55.050 --> 00:54:58.590
Oscar wants to know if anyone's going to organize an office sleepover at the studio.
奥斯卡想知道是否有人打算在摄影棚组织一场办公室留宿活动。

1208
00:54:58.830 --> 00:54:59.270
Yes.
是的。

1209
00:54:59.330 --> 00:55:01.470
We could spend all night and get to the bottom of this.
我们可以通宵达旦，把这件事查个水落石出。

1210
00:55:01.770 --> 00:55:04.210
Then he says, unfortunately, I'm busy on that date.
然后他说，不幸的是，那天我没空。

1211
00:55:04.490 --> 00:55:05.950
The date that hasn't been set.
那个还没定下来的日子。

1212
00:55:07.190 --> 00:55:09.910
Well, I guess the answer is no.
好吧，我想答案是否定的。

1213
00:55:10.330 --> 00:55:14.950
None of us remember or experienced a paranormal experience on the set of the office.
我们中没有人记得或经历过《办公室》片场的灵异事件。

1214
00:55:15.090 --> 00:55:19.690
But I thank you for your question because it has created a very entertaining text thread response.
但我感谢你的提问，因为它引发了一连串非常有趣的短信回复。

1215
00:55:20.350 --> 00:55:22.590
I have my favorite line of this episode.
我有这一集中最喜欢的一句台词。

1216
00:55:22.910 --> 00:55:23.770
What is it?
是什么？

1217
00:55:24.170 --> 00:55:29.410
It's when Robert California notices that Creed is a little nervous around the fake snake.
就是罗伯特·加州注意到克里德在假蛇面前有点紧张的时候。

1218
00:55:29.610 --> 00:55:29.910
Okay.
好的。

1219
00:55:30.250 --> 00:55:32.470
And Robert says, are you scared of snakes?
罗伯特说，你怕蛇吗？

1220
00:55:32.470 --> 00:55:36.810
And Creed says, you don't live as long as I have without a healthy fear of snakes, Bobby.
克里德说，鲍比，像我活这么久的人，不可能不对蛇心存敬畏。

1221
00:55:37.750 --> 00:55:40.010
I just love that Creed called him Bobby.
我就是喜欢克里德叫他鲍比。

1222
00:55:40.290 --> 00:55:41.950
No one else calls him Bobby.
没别人叫他鲍比。

1223
00:55:42.750 --> 00:55:50.610
Well, thus begins a series of little scenes where whoever Robert is talking to, he's getting them to tell him about his fear.
好吧，接下来是一系列小场景，无论罗伯特在和谁说话，他都在诱导对方说出自己的恐惧。

1224
00:55:50.870 --> 00:55:53.530
And Daryl is afraid of being buried alive.
达里尔害怕被活埋。

1225
00:55:53.530 --> 00:55:57.550
And Meredith tells Robert that Jim gives her the creeps.
梅雷迪思告诉罗伯特，吉姆让她感到毛骨悚然。

1226
00:55:58.270 --> 00:56:03.870
And then this cuts to a Robert California talking head where he just says, what am I up to?
然后镜头切到罗伯特·加州的单人访谈，他只是说，我在搞什么名堂？

1227
00:56:04.770 --> 00:56:05.630
Bum, bum, bum.
咚，咚，咚。

1228
00:56:06.070 --> 00:56:10.990
He then launches into a huge, long story.
然后他开始讲一个非常长的故事。

1229
00:56:11.810 --> 00:56:21.310
A creepy, scary story where he singles out every person practically in the bullpen and plays on their fear in his story.
一个令人毛骨悚然的恐怖故事，他在故事里几乎点名了办公区里的每一个人，并利用他们的恐惧大做文章。

1230
00:56:21.310 --> 00:56:23.610
Yes, the story has a snake.
是的，故事里有蛇。

1231
00:56:23.850 --> 00:56:25.630
It has someone being buried alive.
有被人活埋的情节。

1232
00:56:25.790 --> 00:56:27.230
It has mummies.
有木乃伊。

1233
00:56:27.530 --> 00:56:29.450
It has someone dying alone.
有孤独死去的人。

1234
00:56:29.770 --> 00:56:31.450
It has a tall, slim man.
有一个又高又瘦的男人。

1235
00:56:32.130 --> 00:56:32.310
Jim.
吉姆。

1236
00:56:33.190 --> 00:56:33.430
Yeah.
没错。

1237
00:56:33.990 --> 00:56:36.310
And it ends so oddly.
而且结尾非常奇怪。

1238
00:56:36.670 --> 00:56:37.170
Yes.
是的。

1239
00:56:37.490 --> 00:56:41.510
And on that fevered night, she rushed to the nursery, threw open the door.
在那狂热的夜晚，她冲进育婴室，猛地推开门。

1240
00:56:41.930 --> 00:56:43.290
Baby, are you okay?
宝贝，你还好吗？

1241
00:56:43.670 --> 00:56:49.050
Baby sat up slowly, turned to mother and said, I'm fine, bitch.
婴儿慢慢坐起来，转向母亲说，我很好，贱人。

1242
00:56:49.750 --> 00:56:51.670
He, like, lowered his voice.
他当时压低了嗓音。

1243
00:56:52.470 --> 00:56:54.230
It was like, what is happening?
简直就像是，这到底是怎么回事？

1244
00:56:54.710 --> 00:56:57.410
To which his son laughs hysterically.
对此，他的儿子笑得歇斯底里。

1245
00:56:57.870 --> 00:56:58.390
Yes.
是的。

1246
00:56:59.030 --> 00:57:00.650
Everyone is just speechless.
每个人都哑口无言。

1247
00:57:01.170 --> 00:57:01.590
Yeah.
是啊。

1248
00:57:01.950 --> 00:57:06.110
And Robert's going to explain what it was all about in his final talking head.
罗伯特会在最后的单人访谈中解释这一切的含义。

1249
00:57:06.250 --> 00:57:09.330
He says, fear plays an interesting role in our lives.
他说，恐惧在我们生活中扮演着有趣的角色。

1250
00:57:09.490 --> 00:57:11.550
How dare we let it motivate us?
我们怎敢让它来驱使我们？

1251
00:57:11.690 --> 00:57:16.190
How dare we let it into our decision making, into our livelihoods, into our relationships?
我们怎么敢让它影响我们的决策、我们的生计、我们的关系？

1252
00:57:16.790 --> 00:57:17.990
It's funny, isn't it?
真有意思，不是吗？

1253
00:57:17.990 --> 00:57:22.170
We take a day, a year, to dress up in costume and celebrate fear.
我们花一天、一年时间去穿上戏服，庆祝恐惧。

1254
00:57:22.470 --> 00:57:23.450
There you have it.
事情就是这样。

1255
00:57:23.630 --> 00:57:28.850
But this episode is going to end with Bert going over to Toby's desk and firing him.
但这一集结尾会是伯特走到托比的办公桌前解雇他。

1256
00:57:28.990 --> 00:57:32.770
He says, I'm the CEO's son, and you're fired.
他说，我是CEO的儿子，你被解雇了。

1257
00:57:33.110 --> 00:57:34.190
So mean.
太刻薄了。

1258
00:57:34.590 --> 00:57:35.050
I know.
我知道。

1259
00:57:35.130 --> 00:57:36.490
Dwight is pranking Toby.
德怀特在恶搞托比。

1260
00:57:36.790 --> 00:57:38.950
He's, like, laughing silently over the partition.
他就像是在隔板那边无声地大笑。

1261
00:57:39.210 --> 00:57:39.830
So mean.
太刻薄了。

1262
00:57:39.830 --> 00:57:44.650
At 21 minutes and 4 seconds, I noticed two things in Toby's nook.
在21分04秒时，我注意到了托比的小隔间里有两件事。

1263
00:57:45.030 --> 00:57:47.070
One good and one, huh?
一件好的，还有一件……嗯？

1264
00:57:47.450 --> 00:57:50.990
The good one is that there are a bunch of new photos of Toby's daughter on the wall.
好的那件是墙上多了很多托比女儿的新照片。

1265
00:57:51.130 --> 00:57:52.290
I love this detail.
我喜欢这个细节。

1266
00:57:52.490 --> 00:57:56.470
I love how our desks changed with us and with the passage of time.
我喜欢我们的办公桌随着我们和时间的流逝而发生变化。

1267
00:57:56.650 --> 00:57:59.570
You know, he still has his little puppy dog thing.
你知道，他还有那个小狗摆件。

1268
00:57:59.570 --> 00:58:03.990
He has a lot of things that are the same, but all the pictures on the wall.
他有很多东西都没变，但墙上的照片全换了。

1269
00:58:04.170 --> 00:58:05.090
His daughter is older.
他女儿长大了。

1270
00:58:05.630 --> 00:58:08.950
You know, Toby's daughter was played by one of our crew members' daughters,
你知道，托比的女儿是由我们剧组人员的女儿扮演的，

1271
00:58:08.950 --> 00:58:12.270
and that crew member would bring in updated photos for Toby's nook.
那位剧组人员会带更新的照片来装饰托比的小隔间。

1272
00:58:12.470 --> 00:58:13.570
So new pictures.
所以是新照片。

1273
00:58:13.990 --> 00:58:16.610
But also, that brings me to Huh?
但这也让我想到了那个“嗯？”

1274
00:58:16.950 --> 00:58:22.250
Which is on his desk, he has a mug with all of his pens and pencils in it,
就是在他桌上，他有一个放着所有钢笔和铅笔的杯子，

1275
00:58:22.250 --> 00:58:26.090
but it's a yellow NBC Peacock mug.
但那是一个黄色的NBC孔雀台标杯子。

1276
00:58:27.270 --> 00:58:27.770
Whoopsies.
哎呀。

1277
00:58:28.170 --> 00:58:28.630
Huh?
嗯？

1278
00:58:29.730 --> 00:58:30.750
What's that about?
那是怎么回事？

1279
00:58:31.250 --> 00:58:31.750
I don't know.
我不知道。

1280
00:58:31.950 --> 00:58:32.390
I don't know.
我不知道。

1281
00:58:33.750 --> 00:58:35.390
Well, that was spooked, lady.
好吧，刚才真是吓人，女士。

1282
00:58:35.890 --> 00:58:36.310
Yeah.
是啊。

1283
00:58:36.770 --> 00:58:42.230
I think what I learned is there's nothing scarier than Robert California zeroing in on you.
我想我学到的是，没有什么比罗伯特·加利福尼亚盯着你看更可怕的了。

1284
00:58:42.370 --> 00:58:43.550
I think you're right.
我想你是对的。

1285
00:58:45.580 --> 00:58:46.780
I think you're right.
我想你是对的。

1286
00:58:47.000 --> 00:58:48.700
Well, thank you, everyone, for listening.
好了，谢谢大家的收听。

1287
00:58:48.700 --> 00:58:53.880
Thank you to Steve Burgess and the Office Peeps text thread for getting back to us.
感谢史蒂夫·伯吉斯和“办公室伙伴”短信群组回复我们。

1288
00:58:54.440 --> 00:58:57.380
And thanks to you guys for sending in your questions and comments.
也感谢你们发来问题和评论。

1289
00:58:57.500 --> 00:58:58.660
We just love them so much.
我们真的非常喜欢。

1290
00:58:58.740 --> 00:59:00.500
And happy summer, everybody.
祝大家夏天快乐。

1291
00:59:00.640 --> 00:59:02.580
We're going to take two weeks off.
我们要休息两周。

1292
00:59:02.980 --> 00:59:04.300
My birthday is coming up.
我的生日快到了。

1293
00:59:05.340 --> 00:59:08.600
Angela, once again, we will not be working on your birthday.
安吉拉，再说一次，你生日那天我们不会工作的。

1294
00:59:08.620 --> 00:59:09.140
I know.
我知道。

1295
00:59:09.400 --> 00:59:11.160
We won't be working on my birthday.
我生日那天我们不会工作的。

1296
00:59:11.480 --> 00:59:12.180
That's okay.
没关系。

1297
00:59:12.440 --> 00:59:13.800
I'll eat cake for everybody.
我会替大家吃蛋糕的。

1298
00:59:14.600 --> 00:59:16.740
Well, we'll see you in two weeks, everyone.
好吧，两周后见，各位。

1299
00:59:16.980 --> 00:59:17.260
Love you.
爱你们。

1300
00:59:17.800 --> 00:59:18.280
Bye.
再见。

1301
00:59:18.280 --> 00:59:18.640
Bye.
再见。

